Dear National Library, Singapore,

I run Lesser Known Singapore (https://pikaia.github.io and
https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore), a small non-commercial
blog covering overlooked history and lesser-known facts about
Singapore. I'd like to request permission to reproduce two photographs
from your digital collection for an upcoming post about Singapore's
last wild tiger.

Specifically:
- "Three tiger hunters, 1930" =E2=80=94

https://www.nlb.gov.sg/main/image-detail?cmsuuid=3Ddc6cb21a-c53e-4498-b1c9-=
2f3475884260
  (three hunters posing with the dead tiger by the roadside at Choa Chu
  Kang Village, killed 26 October 1930)
- "Tiger hunters, 1930" =E2=80=94

https://www.nlb.gov.sg/main/image-detail?cmsuuid=3Df0385331-c509-4046-b45c-=
b480f416b947
  (a larger group of hunters posing with the same tiger, same location
  and date)

Intended use: as illustrations in a blog post about the history of
wild tigers in Singapore, with full credit given as you advise and a
link back to each record.

Could you let me know the permissions, credit lines, and any
applicable fee for this non-commercial use? Happy to provide any more
detail if useful.

Thank you for your time.

Best regards,
Chris Lee
chriskslee@gmail.com
https://pikaia.github.io
https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore

